NOTICE -- licence record for the scripts/remote remote visual-control tooling.

This record is referenced by scripts/remote/rt-build. It covers the C tools
that rt-build compiles. Reviewed in full by Charmy (TASK-0041 items 9 to 11)
and by the licence gate (scripts/licence-check, CI Licence Check workflow).

--- The team's own sources -----------------------------------------------

scripts/rdp-input.c, scripts/rdp-pointer.c, scripts/remote/uinput-inject.c
and the shell tools in scripts/remote/ are team-authored, Apache-2.0, under
the repository root licence (LICENSE at repo root). Each C file carries its
own licence header. No part of these tools is copied from upstream sources;
they call public FreeRDP 3 client APIs written by the team.

--- What the RDP tools link against --------------------------------------

rdp-input and rdp-pointer link against libfreerdp3 and libfreerdp-client3.
Nothing of FreeRDP's source is vendored, compiled in, or distributed by this
repository. The build links dynamically from distro packages installed by the
operator. The binaries rt-build produces land in $RT_BUILD_DIR (default
~/.cache/team-chaotix/remote-build) and are never committed.

Verified package identity on the controller, 2026-11-22, command
`rpm -q --qf '%{NAME}-%{VERSION}-%{RELEASE} licence=%{LICENSE}\n' freerdp-libs`:

  freerdp-libs-3.32.2-1.el10_2
    licence=Apache-2.0 AND HPND AND LGPL-2.1-or-later
            AND LicenseRef-Fedora-Public-Domain AND OFL-1.1

Upstream FreeRDP (https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP) is dual-licensed
Apache-2.0 or GPL-2.0+. The team's tools take the Apache-2.0 option, which
matches the repository licence and the licence headers in both C files. The
LGPL-2.1+ and HPND terms inside the distro package are satisfied by dynamic
linking against the unmodified distro library, which is what gcc does here.
No FreeRDP source is modified, so no GPL derivative is created.

--- What the uinput injector links against --------------------------------

rt-uinput-inject compiles against kernel UAPI headers only (uinput.h,
input.h, unistd.h and friends). Linux kernel UAPI headers are distributed
under a copyleft-left exception for userspace programs: they do not infect
the program's licence. The injector links no userspace library beyond libc.

--- Third-party data -------------------------------------------------------

None. No game data, no reference CHK file, no harvested asset is stored in
any git-tracked path under scripts/remote/. Evidence directories for captures
live outside the repository.
